From: oveRTOS
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg: clear the jump cache with memset on wasm hosts

tcg_flush_jmp_cache() clears its 4096 entries with one qatomic_set() each.
On a WebAssembly host every atomic store is a sequentially consistent
fence, so a single flush costs tens of microseconds.  A v7-M guest that
reprograms the MPU on every context switch (each MPU_RBAR/MPU_RASR write
flushes the TLB, and with it this cache) spends most of its time here:
in a browser profile of an MPU-isolating FreeRTOS guest, 64% of the vCPU
thread.

The flush runs on the vCPU that owns the cache, or with all vCPUs
stopped, and a concurrent invalidation only ever stores NULL, so a plain
memset() is equivalent.  Limit it to Emscripten builds.

---
--- a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
@@ -632,7 +632,18 @@
         return;
     }
 
+#ifdef EMSCRIPTEN
+    /*
+     * Every wasm atomic store is a full fence, which makes the loop below
+     * cost tens of microseconds; guests that reprogram the v7-M MPU on each
+     * context switch flush thousands of times a second.  The flush runs on
+     * the owning vCPU or with all vCPUs stopped, and a concurrent
+     * invalidation only ever stores NULL, so a plain clear is equivalent.
+     */
+    memset(jc->array, 0, sizeof(jc->array));
+#else
     for (int i = 0; i < TB_JMP_CACHE_SIZE; i++) {
         qatomic_set(&jc->array[i].tb, NULL);
     }
+#endif
 }
